-- title:
--   Localisation at a prime of a surjective ring map
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be commutative rings, let $f : A \to B$ be a ring homomorphism which is surjective as a function, let $\mathfrak p \subset A$ and $\mathfrak q \subset B$ be prime ideals, and assume $\mathfrak p = f^{-1}(\mathfrak q)$, i.e. $\mathfrak p$ equals the contraction `Ideal.comap f q`. Under this hypothesis Mathlib's `Localization.localRingHom p q f hpq` is the induced homomorphism of local rings $f_{\mathfrak p} : A_{\mathfrak p} \to B_{\mathfrak q}$ between the localisations `Localization.AtPrime p` and `Localization.AtPrime q`, characterised by sending $a/s$ to $f(a)/f(s)$. The assertion is the conjunction of two statements: first, $f_{\mathfrak p}$ is surjective; second, the kernel of $f_{\mathfrak p}$, as an ideal of $A_{\mathfrak p}$, equals the image under the localisation map $A \to A_{\mathfrak p}$ of the kernel of $f$, that is, the ideal $(\ker f)A_{\mathfrak p}$ generated by the image of $\ker f$ (`Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime p)) (RingHom.ker f)`).
--
--   This is the ideal-level form of the exactness of localisation: localising a surjection $A \twoheadrightarrow B \cong A/\ker f$ at a prime $\mathfrak p$ lying under $\mathfrak q$ gives $B_{\mathfrak q} \cong A_{\mathfrak p}/(\ker f)A_{\mathfrak p}$. It is used in the treatment of formal smoothness of localisations of polynomial quotients at a prime, via [`MvPolynomial.formallySmooth_localization_atPrime_quotient_of_forall_pderiv_mem`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.formallySmooth_localization_atPrime_quotient_of_forall_pderiv_mem).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Localization_localRingHom_surjective_and_ker_eq_map_of_surjective.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem Localization.localRingHom_surjective_and_ker_eq_map_of_surjective
    {A B : Type} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] (f : A →+* B) (hf : Function.Surjective f)
    (p : Ideal A) [p.IsPrime] (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime] (hpq : p = Ideal.comap f q) :
    Function.Surjective (Localization.localRingHom p q f hpq) ∧
      RingHom.ker (Localization.localRingHom p q f hpq) =
        Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime p)) (RingHom.ker f) := by sorry
